            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0751" n="619" xml:id="pg619"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7560: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-17T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 17,
                                1926—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 17—6:14
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>328. My 317, August 5, noon. Following from American consul at Changsha: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Chiang Kai-shih arrived this morning. There is no serious fighting.
                            Earty renewal of drive toward Hankow is not unlikely. Department has not
                            been informed.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
